# Summarize every finished task

When working through a list of tasks, write a short summary the moment a task
is done — before moving on to the next one. Don't save it all for one summary
at the end of the session.

Mark the todo completed and write the summary in the same step.

## What a summary covers

- What changed, in plain language, and which files or areas it touched
- How it was verified (lint, build, tests, migration run, a real request)
- Anything left unfinished, risky, or worth a decision later

## Shape

Keep it to a few sentences of prose. No headers, no bullet lists, no tables for
a single task — those are for the end-of-session wrap-up across many tasks.

Lead with the outcome:

> Gallery items now have a stable `slug` column, so renaming a title no longer
> breaks a shared link. Touched the entity, service, DTOs and the frontend URL
> builder, plus a migration that backfills `slug` from `title`. Verified with
> lint, both builds, the backend test suite, and a live request to
> `/api/gallery/0057`. Old `/gallery/<title>` links still resolve through a
> fallback lookup.

## Why

The person reading this stepped away while the work ran. A summary that arrives
with each finished task tells them where things stand without reading the whole
transcript, and surfaces a wrong turn while it is still cheap to correct.
